          %title Extended real numbers
          %h1#extended_real_numbers Extended real numbers
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_extended_dedekind_cuts"} As extended Dedekind cuts
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_ratios_of_real_numbers"} As ratios of real numbers
              %li
                %a{:href => "#orders"} Orders
              %li
                %a{:href => "#arithmetic"} Arithmetic
              %li
                %a{:href => "#constructive_aspects"} Constructive aspects
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An extended real number is usually a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi log
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi t
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log(1/t - 1)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0,1]
            (including
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 0,1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tan
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tan t
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            a real number (including an odd multiple of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi/2
          %p
            There are actually two slightly different notions that both go by the name ‘extended real number’: one in which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
            are distinct (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithm
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent"} tangent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient space
            of the former.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Classically, one simply defines an extended real number to be either a real number,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %h3#as_extended_dedekind_cuts As extended Dedekind cuts
          %p
            One way to define extended real numbers is to adjust the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cut"} Dedekind cut
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ≠
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty \ne -\infty
          %p
            So let an
            %strong extended Dedekind cut
            be a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            of sets of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            such that:
          %ul
            %li
              For each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in L
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b
            %li
              For each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in U
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b
            %li
              Whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b
              are rational numbers, either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in L
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in U
              (non-exclusively).
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in L
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in U
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b
          %p (The usual slight variations available in the notion of Dedekind cut apply here as well, in the same ways.)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is empty, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            must be the set of all rational numbers; this extended cut represents
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is empty, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            must be the set of all rational numbers; this extended cut represents
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %strong bounded
            if instead
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            are both
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
          %p
            The space of extended real numbers in this sense is often denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbb{R}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end+compactification"} end compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                line segment
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/line+segment"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %strong extended real number line segment
          %h3#as_ratios_of_real_numbers As ratios of real numbers
          %p
            Another way to define extended real numbers is to represent them as ratios of real numbers. This naturally defines the sort of extended real number in which
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty = -\infty
          %p
            So let a
            %strong nontrivial ratio
            of real numbers be a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
            of real numbers such that either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \ne 0
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \ne 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ne
            we mean the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
            on real numbers.) We write the ratio as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi ∶
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a &amp;#8758; b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mi ∶
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a &amp;#8758; b
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mi ∶
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c &amp;#8758; d
            to be
            = succeed "," do
              %strong equivalent
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi ∶
                    %mi b
                    %mi ∷
                    %mi c
                    %mi ∶
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a &amp;#8758; b &amp;#8759; c &amp;#8758; d
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a d = b c
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            on nontrivial ratios; modulo this equivalence relation, the nontrivial ratios represent extended real numbers.
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \ne 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mi ∶
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a &amp;#8758; b
            is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi b
                  %mi ∶
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a/b &amp;#8758; 1
            and represents the real number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a/b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mi ∶
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a &amp;#8758; 0
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \ne 0
            are all equivalent and represent
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mi ∶
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 &amp;#8758; 0
            is considered trivial and does not represent any extended real number. If we want to include it, then we get a
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wheel"} wheel
          %p
            This is a special case of forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+line"} projective line
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℙ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}\mathbb{R}^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            = succeed "." do
              %strong extended real number circle
          %h2#orders Orders
          %p
            We can put a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbb{R}}
            by setting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty \lt x \lt \infty
            for any real number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            on such cuts.
          %p
            We can put a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+order"} cyclic order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℙ
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}\mathbb{R}^1
            by setting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x,y,z)
            true if any of the following hold:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y \lt z
              are all real numbers,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi z
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \lt z \lt x
              are all real numbers,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \lt x \lt y
              are all real numbers,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \lt z
              are real numbers and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = \infty
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \lt x
              are real numbers and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = \infty
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
              are real numbers and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z = \infty
          %p (These orders can be defined constructively too, with a little more work.)
          %h2#arithmetic Arithmetic
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbb{R}}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty + x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty + \infty
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            a real number) and similarly
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x - \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty + x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo −
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty - \infty
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
            are opposites (additive inverses). These are all straightforward extensions of the usual definition of addition for Dedekind cuts. However, when we try
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo −
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty - \infty
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty + \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\empty,\empty)
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℙ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}\mathbb{R}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + \infty
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo +
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty + x
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            a real number). Now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            is its own opposite. These all agree with the additive rule
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi ∶
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mi ∶
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mi c
                    %mi ∶
                    %mi b
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a &amp;#8758; b) + (c &amp;#8758; d) = (a d + b c &amp;#8758; b d)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty + \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mi ∶
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 &amp;#8758; 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty + \infty = \infty
            is also widely seen, I think.)
          %p
            Note that although we have blithely referred to ‘additive inverses’, addition does not form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            in either case. The reason is that the opposites of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            are not really additive inverses, since the result of the relevant addition is undefined rather than zero. (If you define the sum to be zero so that they become inverses, then you lose associativity; ultimately, there is no way to make a group, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 + \infty = 1 + \infty
            shows that the operation is not cancellative.)
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\mathbb{R}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot {\pm \infty}
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm \infty
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt 0
            but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∓
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot {\pm \infty} = \mp \infty
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is infinite too.) But now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot {\pm \infty}
            is undefined. (Many sources define this to be zero, although I think this is really because they are using
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot \infty = 0
            in the nonnegative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+reals"} lower reals
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℙ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}\mathbb{R}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot \infty
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            as long as
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot \infty
            is undefined (although it is defined in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wheel"} wheel
            over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/\infty = 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/0 = \infty
            to define division, but again these are not really multiplicative inverses. (With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot 1 = 0 \cdot 2
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty \cdot 1 = \infty \cdot 2
          %h2#constructive_aspects Constructive aspects
          %p
            The definitions as phrased above give us
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+real+number"} located
            extended real numbers. We can of course consider unlocated extended real numbers, either
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-sided+real+number"} one-sided
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MacNeille+real+number"} MacNeille
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\infty
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ≠
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty \ne -\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            shows up constructively (especially if only one of them appears), then this is a sign that one may want to generalise to one-sided (or even MacNeille) reals.
          %p
            This has implications for arithmetic; for example, while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \cdot \infty
            is undefined in the extended located real numbers (and in the MacNeille real numbers), it is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            in the nonnegative lower real numbers (and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            in the extended nonnegative upper real numbers).
